    "renderedFields": {
      "description": "<h2>Background</h2><p>The Booking API currently allows a guest to create a reservation without validating that the check-out date is after the check-in date. Support has raised <b>14 tickets</b> in the last sprint from this. See the <a href='#'>design doc</a></p><h2>Requirements</h2><ul><li>POST /booking must reject a reservation where checkout &lt;= checkin with HTTP 400.</li><li>The error body must name the offending field.</li><li>PATCH /booking/{id} must apply the same rule when either date changes.</li><li>Existing reservations that already violate the rule must not be broken by the change.</li></ul><h2>Error contract</h2><table><tr><th>Case</th><th>Status</th><th>Code</th></tr><tr><td>checkout before checkin</td><td>400</td><td>DATE_RANGE_INVALID</td></tr><tr><td>checkout equals checkin</td><td>400</td><td>DATE_RANGE_ZERO</td></tr></table><h2>Sample response</h2><pre>{ \"error\": \"DATE_RANGE_INVALID\", \"field\": \"checkout\" }</pre><p>Rate limiting is already applied at the gateway. Do not add a second limiter.</p><hr/><p>Perf target: p95 under 300ms at 50 rps.</p><p>Legacy clients send dates as epoch millis.</p>"
    }
  },
